      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg by mouth four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is about double the maximum adult daily dose (3,200 mg/day). The single dose of 1,600 mg is also double the usual 800 mg maximum per dose. At these doses, the risks include gastrointestinal bleeding, kidney injury, cardiovascular events, and fluid retention, even with normal baseline function.\n\nIt's possible the intended regimen is different, such as 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum) or 400 to 800 mg every 6 to 8 hours, but that is a prescribing decision.\n\nBecause this is a medication order, a licensed prescriber on the medicine service should review and enter it. If the prescriber confirms a specific dose and frequency, I can enter that order, or they can enter it directly in the order-entry system. If the 1600 mg dose came from a written source, such as a protocol or a transcribed order, please have the prescriber check it against the original before anything is given."
      }
